# ADR-001: Table Format Selection

## Status
Accepted

## Context
The Bronze lakehouse layer requires a table format to sit on top of
object storage and provide ACID transactions, schema evolution, and
MERGE support. The selection criteria were engine compatibility,
ecosystem openness, and broad market relevance.

## Decision
Apache Iceberg was selected over Delta Lake as the table format
for this project.

## Reasoning
Iceberg is engine-agnostic and built on open standards, providing
native compatibility across Spark, Flink, Trino, and DuckDB without
vendor lock-in. While Delta Lake offers tighter out-of-box integration
within the Databricks ecosystem, Iceberg's ecosystem neutrality better
serves the portfolio objective of broad market appeal. Iceberg is
production-standard at organisations including Apple, Netflix, and
Snowflake, and is natively supported by AWS Glue — the catalog
selected for this project's production environment.

## Consequences
**Positive:**
- Compatible with any major compute engine
- Natively supported by AWS Glue, Snowflake, and Databricks
- Positions the project for broad DE and AI engineering role relevance

**Risks and limitations:**
- Slightly less out-of-box tooling than Delta Lake in Databricks-
  specific environments
- Databricks-focused roles may expect Delta Lake familiarity —
  mitigated by the transferability of core table format concepts